==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʌɡ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-ug.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌɡ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|ugge}}, from {{der|en|non|uggr||fear, apprehension, dread}}, related to {{cog|non|ógn||terror, threat, dispute}} and {{m|non|agi||terror, strife, fear, punishment}}. More at {{l|en|awe}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|ugg}}, {{l|en|oug}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|North England|and|Scotland|obsolete}} A feeling of [[fear]], [[horror]] or [[disgust]].
#: {{usex|en|He took an '''ug''' at's meht.}}<!-- as used in The English Dialect Dictionary -->
# {{lb|en|North England|and|Scotland|obsolete}} An object of [[disgust]].
#: {{usex|en|What an '''ug''' ye've myed yorsel.}}<!-- as used in The English Dialect Dictionary -->
# {{lb|en|North England|and|Scotland|obsolete}} [[vomit|Vomited]] matter.
# {{lb|en|Northumbria}} A [[surfeit]].

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|fear; horror}} {{l|en|dread}}, {{l|en|fright}}; see also [[Thesaurus:fear]]
* {{sense|digust}} {{l|en|distaste}}, {{l|en|loathsomeness}}, {{l|en|revulsion}}
* {{sense|object of disgust}} {{l|en|abomination}}
* {{sense|vomit}} {{l|en|chunder}}, {{l|en|sick}}; see also [[Thesaurus:vomit]]
* {{sense|surfeit}} {{l|en|glut}}, {{l|en|surplus}}; see also [[Thesaurus:excess]]

